  "full_review": "# Independent arithmetic template audit\n\nCLEAN/ACCEPT. Full source, audit and publication note read. A restricted independent prefix reader checked all10 new Circuit definitions against the live Code254 expressions after only the declared helper renaming. All11 live templates also match Numeric254 and pinned upstream Codes254.v exactly. The JSON records the exact expressions and file hashes. No Lean build or source edit was performed.\n\n`Circuit.graph` is sound by the stated structural induction. A finite node binds both child values inclusively by the parent output and invokes the exact tagged graph; `tagged_components` supplies both witnesses. Input and constant1 cases are direct equations. This remains correct at output0 and for externally nonstandard elements of any IOpen model. The syntax is one fixed parameter-free Semisentence for each circuit, not a theorem obtained merely from parameter-allowing model definability.\n\nEvery helper matches relative falsity1: neg is implication to1; conj and ex are exactly the original wn/wim/wal expansions. rho8 retains a,b,c,u order; rho6 and all equality occurrences remain native and literal. Container and collection parentheses match exactly. The full bundle is `(C\u2227G)\u2227(membership-vacuity\u2227equality-vacuity)` with no label freshening or new primitive Bottom.\n\nThe positive bundle graph is total even for coincident labels. This intentionally leaves c\u2260a and c\u2260b outside the graph; it does not justify an ungated bundle proof row. Output bounds do not cover arbitrary rejected-row intermediates when the row returns0, and neither module nor note claims the complete row/history/PA theorem.\n\nThe graph compiler unfolds finite syntax recursively; it does not implement a coded DAG evaluator or runtime static sharing. For comparison only, expanded primitive occurrence/distinct counts are C31/26, G24/23, fullbundle72/61, with literal F treated as an atomic constant. Charging one explicit shared F constructor gives27/24/62 shared records, respectively; this is not a state bound. rho1\u20138 have5/6/5/5/5/6/5/6 shared records under that convention. All41 axiom probes and36 callers have the advertised scope, including10 generic graphs,10 all-Nat equalities/live-function interfaces and zero/coincident-label controls. The author's kernelPASS evidence was read, not repeated.\n",
  "root_review": "Read all271 source lines and independent extraction audit, fixed finite Circuit graph/bounds and exact Code254 matches; read maintained runner and scope note. Accepted as positive fixed graphs, not represented gated evaluator/history."
